  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Hash URIs are not properly cleaned up. For example:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "INSERT {",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "<> dc:creator <#creator>.",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "<#creator> a foaf:Person ; foaf:name \"me\" .",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "} WHERE { }",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Now delete the properties of the hash URI (but not the <> dc:creator <#creator> triple):",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "DELETE WHERE { <#creator> ?p ?o . }",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Now I get a 404 for the container even though it is still listed in the parent container. (I can delete the container with CURL, but the HTML UI is useless).",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The issue has to do with the removeEmptyFragments function in FedoraResourceImpl and the way it deletes the \"#\" node if it doesn't contain any properties. But doing so results in a jcr.ItemNotFoundException because of the existence of the `<> dc:creator <#creator>` triple (and possibly other references).",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
   "type": "doc",
   "version": 1
  },
