  "description": "<p>Hash URIs are not properly cleaned up. For example:</p>\n\n<p>INSERT </p>\n{\r\n  &lt;&gt; dc:creator &lt;#creator&gt;.\r\n  &lt;#creator&gt; a foaf:Person ; foaf:name \"me\" .\r\n}\n<p> WHERE { }</p>\n\n<p>Now delete the properties of the hash URI (but not the &lt;&gt; dc:creator &lt;#creator&gt; triple):</p>\n\n<p>DELETE WHERE </p>\n{ &lt;#creator&gt; ?p ?o . }\n\n<p>Now I get a 404 for the container even though it is still listed in the parent container. (I can delete the container with CURL, but the HTML UI is useless).</p>\n\n<p>The issue has to do with the removeEmptyFragments function in FedoraResourceImpl and the way it deletes the \"#\" node if it doesn't contain any properties. But doing so results in a jcr.ItemNotFoundException because of the existence of the `&lt;&gt; dc:creator &lt;#creator&gt;` triple (and possibly other references).</p>",
